{"request_sha256": "b244d783b22256d4aa0b0335843bb0e0378b067b4d8cfe517a9217c2247eb135", "prompt_sha256": "847dd718e56258447ec5fcc89fdaadc9701165d02eab0b51001e616ebc1a0329", "dispatched_prompt_sha256": "f263ee10b24ff74db1826721df8b0d5caec13ac79252a229de4992d0d12e79fa", "schema_sha256": "b11348cd1fb9f87dee1f7d8b64746455da08f64a4885c641943f00ea25a47f5f", "model": "opus", "model_identity_basis": "claude CLI result event modelUsage key: claude-opus-5-5", "effort": "medium", "status": "ok", "forbidden_tools": [], "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 4998}, "answer": {"passes": ["fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass", "pass", "pass"], "defects": ["Seeds 1 and 42 (render-0, render-1): the crown is a small, compact starburst of about 20 short, thin fronds. In reference-0, long fronds form a large rounded crown and the lowest ones hang well below the crown base. In the renders, the crown spread is only about a quarter of the trunk height and the lowest fronds barely droop. This fails owner-fronds-long-arching and crown-pinnate-arching-fronds.", "Leaflets (render-0, render-1, render-2) are short, lozenge-shaped blades lying almost flat along each rachis. The long, narrow, stiff leaflets set at different angles in reference-0 and reference-1, which make each frond look V-shaped and bristly, do not appear. This fails leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow.", "Trunk (render-2) is a smooth dark column with only a few small, isolated knobs. It has no spiral, diamond-shaped lattice of leaf-base stubs like reference-1 and reference-2. This fails trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern.", "Close base view (render-3) is smooth bark with four isolated knobs. It has no dense stub lattice and none of the reddish-brown fibre mat seen in reference-2. This fails trunk-fibrous-matting and leaf-base-close.", "No hanging orange fruit bunches appear in render-0 or render-1. Reference-0 shows two or three bunches, and the frozen inventory lists fruit-clusters-pendent as a core trait."], "observations": ["Both whole-tree renders show one unbranched trunk with a crown of fronds at the top. There are no side branches, and nothing grows on the trunk.", "render-0: the trunk is straight and almost the same width all the way up, with a flared base. render-1: the trunk leans slightly and curves one way, with the curve getting stronger just below the crown. It is not wavy.", "The knobs on the trunk appear to be leaf-base stubs from the trunk organs (fn-110), not growth. They are sparse and do not form the lattice pattern.", "render-2 shows the crown more closely: the fronds do arch outward and down somewhat, but they are still short and their leaflets are small.", "render-3 is marked 'hidden' in the metadata, but the image clearly shows the trunk surface. It has a hard, flat split between light and shadow down the middle.", "The finish of render-0 and render-1 (clean shading, cast shadow) is roughly as good as the spruce quality anchor (anchor-0). The anchor was used for finish only, not for shape.", "The date cluster (fn-111) has not landed, so the missing fruit is a known gap in the generator. It is still a mismatch against a core reference trait."], "findings": [{"observation": "The crown's fronds are short and thin, and the crown is small compared with the trunk. Only a few of the lowest fronds tip below the crown base, and none of them droop the way the fronds in reference-0 do.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Possibly because the frond length and leaflet size settings are too low. This is the owner's own guess, and it is untested."}, {"observation": "Leaflets are short blades lying flat along each rachis. They are not the long, narrow, stiff leaflets set at different angles seen in the references.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The trunk surface is smooth, with only a few isolated knobs. There is no spiral diamond pattern of stubs and no fibre mat.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The checklist says the generator does not yet produce this trunk texture."}, {"observation": "No fruit bunches are present.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "The date cluster (fn-111) has not landed. Fruit is also seasonal, so the inventory marking it as a core trait may be too strict. The mismatch is reported rather than dismissed."}, {"observation": "The seed 1 trunk is straight and the seed 42 trunk leans with a single curve. Both are close to constant width and neither is wavy.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Seed 42's curve is sharpest just below the crown, close to a kink. It does not reverse direction, so it counts as a gentle lean within the range reference-0 shows.", "evidence_ids": ["render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "No plants or other growth appear on the trunk in either seed. The small knobs are trunk-organ stubs.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "There is no skirt of dead fronds and no orange sheath at the petiole bases. Both are secondary traits.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "The fronds do come out from one point at the top and form a rough rosette. But they are short and thin and the crown is small. They lack the long arching fronds and drooping lower fronds of reference-0."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Leaflets are short, lozenge-shaped and lie almost flat, not long, narrow and stiff. The fronds do not have the V-shaped, bristly look of the references."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Only a few isolated, rounded knobs appear on a smooth trunk. There is no spiral, diamond-shaped lattice of wedge-shaped stubs."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The render shows smooth, flat bark. There is no matted reddish-brown fibre between stubs."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Both seeds have a single unbranched stem of almost constant width."}, {"trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "No hanging fruit bunches appear in either render. The date cluster (fn-111) has not landed. Fruit is seasonal, but this core trait is reported rather than dismissed."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/home/daniel/Projects/telperion/.worktrees/fn-80-the-gap-loops-first-live-run","session_id":"ec380c35-24e3-4e53-9c72-1b7b258c5cfa","tools":["StructuredOutput"],"mcp_servers":[],"model":"claude-opus-5-5","permissionMode":"default","slash_commands":["deep-research","design","design-sync","dataviz","update-config","verify"